182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 647 0 R
/E (Large Language Models \(LLMs\), Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\) and tool-using AI agents are widely used for document question answering and task automation, but fluent responses do not guarantee factual accuracy, evidence grounding or correct tool execution. Failures can originate in irrelevant retrieval, unsupported claims, incorrect tool selection or inefficient execution, and manual inspection of final answers alone cannot reliably identify their causes. This project proposes an integrated platform to evaluate and observe RAG-based agents using a controlled test dataset. Each run is designed to capture the query, retrieved passages and similarity scores, tool calls, model response, latency, token usage and errors. The evaluation combines deterministic checks, LLM-as-a-Judge and a small human-validated sample to assess retrieval quality, answer relevance, faithfulness, tool selection and task completion. A dashboard will support trace inspection, failure analysis, model and prompt comparison, and repeatable regression testing. Actual performance results will be added after experiments are executed.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
