189 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 652 0 R
/E (Large Language Models can generate natural-language answers, while Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\) connects them to external documents and AI agents extend them through multi-step decisions and tool calls. Yet reliability depends on every stage: retrieving relevant evidence, selecting and using tools correctly, generating supported answers, and completing tasks within acceptable time and resource limits. This project aims to design an integrated platform for systematically evaluating and monitoring RAG-based agents. It will use a controlled dataset, capture detailed execution traces, measure retrieval and answer quality, assess tool selection and task completion, track latency, token usage and failures, compare model and prompt versions, and present findings through a dashboard to support diagnosis and regression testing.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
